//! On2 VP6 video decoder for the EA `MVhd` movies (`video/*/*.vp6`).
//!
//! The game links On2's VP6 decoder (`VP6_LoadFrame` 0x802a289c, `VP6_DecodeFrameMbs` 0x802a08fc,
//! `VP6_PredictFilteredBlock` 0x8029bc54, ...); every constant table used here is copied from it
//! (`vp6_tables.rs`, generated by tools/extract_vp6_tables.py).  The bitstream procedures follow that decoder:
//! * header (`VP6_LoadFrame`): frame type, 6-bit quantizer, multi-stream flag; key frames add version (5 bits), profile
//!   (2 bits), interlace flag, the second-partition offset, and macroblock rows/columns through the bool decoder;
//! * profile 0 (all movies here) never reads filter or loop-filter fields, and `VP6_PredictFilteredBlock` then uses the
//!   bilinear predictor without the in-loop deblock copy;
//! * macroblock-type deltas (`VP6_decodeModeDiff`: 205, 171, 83, 199, 140, 125, 104 and 4 x 7 bits);
//! * coefficient tokens, DC prediction, the VP3/VP6 integer IDCT (DC-only add `(dc + 15) >> 5`).
//! The picture is coded bottom-up; frames are returned top-down.
use crate::vp6_tables as t;

